SP COBOL is made of two kinds of code under two licenses.

1. compiler/  -- GPL version 3 or later (see compiler/COPYING).
   The compiler is GnuCOBOL 3.2 (Copyright Free Software Foundation, Inc.)
   with a C# back end added. compiler/gnucobol-3.2-csharp.patch and the
   changed files in compiler/cobc/ are covered by the GPL like the rest of
   GnuCOBOL. The cobc.exe shipped inside the SDK package is built from
   GnuCOBOL 3.2 plus that patch.

2. Everything else (runtime/, sdk/, editor/, templates/, tools/, samples/,
   docs) -- the MIT License below.

Programs you write and build with SP COBOL are yours; neither license
applies to them.

